 # SVG Texture
 
 ## What it is
-- **`UWidgetSVGTexture`** ("SVG Texture", `NameTBD/Widgets/WidgetSVGTexture.h`): a **`UTexture2D` subclass** made by importing a `.svg`. Widgets use it as any texture (Brush Resource, `SetBrushFromTexture`, button styles): import the SVG, set it on the brush. Nothing in UMG/Slate knows it was an SVG.
-- **Fidelity:** drawn on import (editor only) into the texture's source pixels at **Resolution Scale** (default 4) x the SVG's own size (width/height, else viewBox), the longest side held to **Max Resolution** (default 2048). UI settings set in the constructor: `TC_EditorIcon` (uncompressed RGBA), sRGB, `TEXTUREGROUP_UI`, Never Stream, **mips (`TMGS_SimpleAverage`)** - so it is sharp at and below Resolution Scale x its size and filters cleanly when drawn smaller. The brush's Image Size on drop is the texture's size (Resolution Scale x the SVG size), as for any texture.
-- **Colours (the "black SVG" fix):** **Colors** (`TArray<FWidgetSVGColor>`, `EditFixedSize`) lists every colour the SVG uses (fills, strokes, gradient stops; first-use order; opacity left out) with **Draw As** next to it, edited inline in the texture's Details. Draw As alpha multiplies the SVG's own opacity. **Draw In White (Tint With Brush)** (`bDrawInWhite`, default off) draws every colour white keeping opacity, so the Brush Tint / Color and Opacity colours it. A shape with no fill is black in SVG: that is the black entry.
-- **Redraw:** editing Resolution Scale, Max Resolution, Draw In White or Colors redraws from `SVGSource` (the file's text, kept in the asset) and rebuilds the texture (not while a picker/spin box is dragged: `Interactive` changes are skipped). Undo redraws from the restored settings. Reimport reads the file again, keeping each still-present colour's Draw As.
-- Editor-only data: `SVGSource`, `Colors`, the settings, `SVGSize`. A cooked game has only the texture.
+- **`UWidgetSVGTexture`** ("SVG Texture", `NameTBD/Widgets/WidgetSVGTexture.h`): a `UObject` asset made by importing a `.svg`, that **owns a `UTexture2D` subobject** (`Texture`, the SVG as drawn, cooked with the asset) and implements **`ISlateTextureAtlasInterface`** (`GetSlateAtlasData`: the whole texture), as a Paper2D sprite does. So it is picked as a Brush's Image (Brush Resource allows Texture, Material and Slate Texture Atlas Interface) on an Image, a Border, a button style...: import the SVG, set it on the brush. Blueprint: `Set Brush From Atlas Interface`, or **`GetTexture`** for anything that wants a Texture 2D.
